sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-teissieri-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-teissieri-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-teissieri-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila teissieri Turing wavelength at 1.7 µm (detail scale s0, Holocene 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 87.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the same Schnakenberg patch (λ_c formula = 1.72 µm, dispersion Pearson r = 0.9935, RMSE = 0.030 1/s) and adds the two Pass-1 measurements that were missing. The growth-rate peak is at 1.985 µm; the saturated sub-bin wavelength is 1.903 µm, 4.2% shorter than that peak and 10.6% longer than the determinant-minimising formula wavelength. Those are reported as separate numbers. The rendered-frame KS against the specimen is 0.147 (reference 0.05); the raw-activator KS is 0.450. Canonical CV similarity is 88.4 on the 12-frame 800×600 GIF. R3 stays open: one assessor, and no Commons bitmap exists for this species. Overall 87.9/100 (faithfulness 87.9, reproducibility 87.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 87, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_teissieri_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-teissieri-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 475296 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 3afee39d65af76a252cc08a982ab25bf93da7d9e7f64ba49f32fe573813cd6dd (sha256 3afee39d65af76a252cc08a982ab25bf93da7d9e7f64ba49f32fe573813cd6dd), spec_fingerprint eae547f9e47b2ea29de70862c97589eafea17d3c75744f5144aa5ef1d4f3d6d0. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: eae547f9e47b2ea29de70862c97589eafea17d3c75744f5144aa5ef1d4f3d6d0; artifact_sha256: 3afee39d65af76a252cc08a982ab25bf93da7d9e7f64ba49f32fe573813cd6dd. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-teissieri-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical wavenumber and the unequal-diffusivity condition. | Schnakenberg 1979 reaction terms a - u + u^2 v and b - u^2 v. | Tsacas 1971 name Drosophila teissieri, confirmed at GBIF 5074619.; reconstructed_in_script: (a, b, gamma, Dv/Du) = (0.13, 0.91, 1.15, 17.4) so the formula wavelength is 1.72 µm. | σ(k) peak, rendered-frame KS, equal-diffusion and autocatalysis ablations, diffusivity sweep.; transfer_boundary: 1.72 µm is the campaign detail-scale assignment, not a published teissieri measurement. | Predecessor 97.6 µm and successor floor 2.72 µm are atlas contrasts at 0 Ma.; does_not_claim: That the nonlinear pattern must sit on the formula wavelength. It tracks the growth-rate peak (1.985 µm) more closely than the determinant shortcut (1.72 µm). | That D. virilis descends from D. teissieri. | That a second assessor or a Commons photograph was obtained.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [independent_assessor/specimen-match, pressure P=0.5]: A second assessor and a CC-licensed taxonomic photograph, if one is later released, would be the only honest way to raise specimen-match further.",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Resolved in this pass. Growth-rate peak is 1.985 µm; saturated wavelength is 1.903 µm (relative gap 0.042). Formula λ_c remains 1.72 µm and is not overwritten.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Resolved in this pass. rendered_frame_ks compares the composite frame to the specimen. Activator-vs-micrograph KS is retained as a separate, larger distance.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Still open. One builder-assessor, and Wikimedia Commons had no CC bitmap of Drosophila teissieri on 2026-10-27, so the gallery micrograph remains the specimen.', 'status': 'open'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.879"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; R3 second assessor still open)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

